chat-to-cop -- AI Staff Officer for MASH Wargame Events
=======================================================

This is a self-contained package for the chat-to-cop pipeline. It
monitors IRC chat channels from a MASH/DASH exercise, uses a local
LLM to extract world-state information (tracks, fuel, weapons,
taskings, CSAR events), and writes structured updates to a database.

The package includes a demo mode with canned exercise messages so you
can see it working immediately. No internet connection required.


PREREQUISITES

  - Docker Desktop (Windows, Mac, or Linux)
    https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/
  - No other software is needed


QUICK START

  Linux / Mac:
    cd chat-to-cop-portable
    bash start.sh

  Windows:
    cd chat-to-cop-portable
    start.bat

  First startup takes 30-60 seconds while the LLM model loads into
  memory. Once ready, the pipeline begins processing demo messages
  automatically.


WHAT YOU WILL SEE

  The pipeline connects to a mock IRC server that replays canned
  exercise messages (fuel reports, weapons status, CSAR events, ISR
  contacts, STT voice transcriptions). For each message, the LLM
  extracts structured data and writes it to a SQLite database.

  Watch the pipeline logs:
    docker compose logs -f pipeline

  Browse the REST API:
    http://localhost:8001/docs


CONNECTING TO A REAL IRC SERVER

  To use with a real MASH/DASH IRC server instead of the demo:

  1. Edit docker-compose.yml
  2. In the pipeline service, change CHAT_TO_COP_IRC_URL from
     ws://mock-irc:8097 to your real IRC server, e.g.:
       CHAT_TO_COP_IRC_URL: ws://10.5.185.72:8097
  3. Update CHAT_TO_COP_IRC_CHANNELS if needed
  4. Remove the mock-irc service (or just leave it -- it won't
     interfere if the pipeline points elsewhere)
  5. Remove "mock-irc" from depends_on in the pipeline service
  6. Run: docker compose up -d


GPU VS CPU

  The default configuration uses an NVIDIA GPU for LLM inference.
  This is significantly faster (sub-second vs 30-60 second responses).

  If you do not have an NVIDIA GPU, or if Docker cannot see it:
    Linux/Mac:  bash start.sh --no-gpu
    Windows:    start.bat --no-gpu

  CPU mode works on any machine but inference is much slower. The
  pipeline will still process all messages -- it just takes longer.

  For GPU support on Docker Desktop:
    - Windows: Install NVIDIA drivers and enable WSL2 GPU support
    - Linux: Install nvidia-container-toolkit


STOPPING

  Linux/Mac:  bash start.sh --stop
  Windows:    start.bat --stop

  Or from any terminal:  docker compose down


PORTS

  11434   Ollama LLM API (internal use)
  8097    Mock IRC server (demo mode only)
  8001    REST API + interactive docs

  If any port is already in use on your machine, edit
  docker-compose.yml and change the left side of the port mapping
  (e.g., "8001:8000" to "9001:8000").


TROUBLESHOOTING

  "Docker is not running"
    Start Docker Desktop. On Linux, run: sudo systemctl start docker

  "Port already in use"
    Another program is using port 11434, 8097, or 8001. Either stop
    that program or edit docker-compose.yml to use different ports.

  "GPU not detected" or deploy error
    Run with --no-gpu flag. GPU support requires NVIDIA drivers and
    nvidia-container-toolkit.

  Pipeline shows connection errors
    The pipeline starts before ollama finishes loading the model.
    Wait 30-60 seconds and check logs again. It will retry
    automatically.

  "No space left on device"
    The Docker images are large (~5-8 GB total). Free disk space or
    run: docker system prune

  How to check service status:
    docker compose ps
    docker compose logs ollama
    docker compose logs pipeline


FILE STRUCTURE

  chat-to-cop-portable/
    README.txt              This file
    start.sh                Start script (Linux/Mac)
    start.bat               Start script (Windows)
    docker-compose.yml      Service definitions
    .env                    Configuration (model, channels)
    images/
      chat-to-cop.tar       Pipeline Docker image
      ollama-with-model.tar Ollama + pre-loaded model weights
    data/                   Created at runtime, holds SQLite database
